<title>SOUTH AFRICA: SAfrica Q3 construction work in hand rises 1.9 pct.</title>
<headline>SAfrica Q3 construction work in hand rises 1.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The total value of work in hand by construction firms during the third quarter of 1996 rose 1.9 percent to a seasonally adjusted 13.4 billion rand compared with 13.1 billion rand in the second quarter, the Central Statistical Service (CSS) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>But during the same period the total value of work done fell 3.2 percent to a seasonally adjusted 6.6 billion rand from 6.8 billion rand in the second quarter, the CSS said.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom 27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
